  "diagramType": "use_case",
  "difficulty": "Easy",
  "domain": "Public Library",
  "statement": "A public library wants a self-service kiosk where a Library Member can Borrow Book or Return Book. Both actions always require the system to Scan Library Card first. If a returned book is past its due date, the kiosk may optionally Pay Late Fee. A Librarian can also Restock Returned Books.",
  "deliverables": [
    "Identify the primary and supporting actors.",
    "Model the core user goals inside the system boundary.",
    "Distinguish mandatory sub-flows from optional extensions."
  ],
  "hints": [
    "Library Member interacts with Borrow Book and Return Book via plain associations.",
    "Since both Borrow Book and Return Book always require Scan Library Card, draw «include» from each toward Scan Library Card.",
    "Pay Late Fee only happens conditionally during Return Book, so Pay Late Fee «extend»s Return Book."
  ],
